<!--
    Type-recovery campaign, gzip -O2 (stripped): `gzip_base_name` @0xd290 is
    `endbr64; jmp last_component` - it hands its own rdi to the callee and
    returns what the callee returns - and kuna printed

        void sub_d290(void) { sub_dfd0(); } // tail-call

    while recovering the callee as `char *sub_dfd0(char *a0)` in the same run.
    DWARF says `char *gzip_base_name(char const *fname)`.  coreutils df
    `dir_name` (`call mdir_name; test %rax,%rax; ...`) is the same shape without
    the tail call.

    Root cause (P4, active-input trial scoring).  A call's argument trials come
    from `Heritage::guardCalls` (heritage.cc:1444), one per HERITAGED storage
    range, and a range is heritaged only when some op of the function reads or
    writes it.  `fwd` and `fwdtest` below never name rdi, so their calls get no
    rdi trial, no argument, and neither function gets the parameter it
    forwards.  Where rdi is heritaged, `AncestorRealistic::execute`
    (funcdata_varnode.cc:2159) refuses an input Varnode at the call slot anyway.

    THIS FIXTURE IS THE NEGATIVE CONTROL for the clause that decides the
    argument.  `option passthrough on` adds a forwarded register only when the
    CALLEE's own recovered prototype reads it, and that prototype reaches a
    call site only through `protoorder`, which parks it when a whole-binary
    `decompile-all` decompiles the callee first.  This harness decompiles ONE
    function from a byte image: no callee was decompiled first, `target` has
    stated nothing about itself, and a rule that adds an argument may not read
    silence as evidence.  `park_recovered_proto` is written true only in
    decompiler/crates/kuna-cli/src/decompile_all.rs; the console paths this
    harness runs through (kuna-console/src/project.rs, project_stream.rs) pass
    false, so no stage test can put a parked prototype in front of the rule.
    Both passes therefore render the forwarding functions without the
    parameter.

    The POSITIVE witness is the same code as a real program,
    decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/passthrough_x86_64 (source
    beside it), under `make test-cli`:
    tests/cli/passthrough-gives-a-forwarding-function-its-parameter.json
    renders `char * sub_401019(char *a0) { return sub_401000(a0); }` and
    `void sub_40101b(char *a0)`, and keeps the clobbered and variadic controls
    unchanged; tests/cli/passthrough-off-leaves-the-forwarded-register-unread.json
    is its option-off arm.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "active-input-trial-scoring".  The P0 assertion
    `option passthrough on|off` decides whether a register the function
    forwards untouched to a callee whose recovered prototype reads it is an
    argument (and the function's parameter).  Pass 1 pins the shipped `off`;
    pass 2 pins that `on` alone, with nothing stated, adds nothing.
-->
